      <h1 id="installing-customizing" class="group scroll-mt-20">Customizing nodes<a href="#installing-customizing" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="/_attributes/common-attributes.md"></p>
      <p>You can customize nodes both cluster-wide and per-machine configuration through Ignition, which allows arbitrary partitioning and file content changes to the operating system.</p>
      <p>If a configuration file is documented in {"{"}{"{"} op_system_base_full {"}"}{"}"}, you can modify the file through Ignition.</p>
      <p>There are two ways to deploy machine config changes:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Creating machine configs that are included in manifest files to start up a cluster during <code>openshift-install</code>.</li>
      <li>Creating machine configs that are passed to running OpenShift Container Platform nodes through the Machine Config Operator.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Additionally, modifying the reference config, such as the Ignition config that is passed to <code>coreos-installer</code> when installing bare-metal nodes allows per-machine configuration. The Machine Config Operator cannot yet see these changes.</p>
      <p>The following sections describe features that you might want to configure on your nodes.</p>
